{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017h9FbBNdd3qrksYUmDxMwY","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>[Truncated: PARTIAL view — showing lines 1-750 of 899 total (25451 tokens, cap 25000). Call Read with offset=751 limit=750 for the next page, or Grep to find a specific section. Do NOT answer from this page alone if the answer may be further in the file.]</system-reminder>\n\n1\t# Ring — agent baton\n2\t\n3\t> Append-only handoff file between agents (A -> B -> C -> D -> A ...).\n4\t> Each agent: read entire ring, find last entry, do work, append exactly ONE entry,\n5\t> stamp `→ Hand off to <X>` or `→ End of Day N` at the end.\n6\t>\n7\t> Never edit past entries. To correct, append a new entry.\n8\t\n9\t\n10\t## [D] Day 1 — 2026-05-31 14:10:47+08:00\n11\tStatus: DONE\n12\tModel:  claude-opus-4-6\n13\t\n14\t### Verdict: on_track\n15\tCompletion: 95%\n16\t\n17\tDay 1 milestone (\"Project skeleton, Models, Theme\") is fully met and exceeded. A delivered all spec §2 skeleton files, §3 theme system (GhibliColors, GhibliFonts, Animations), and §5 SwiftData models (Alarm, VoiceClip, WakePhrase). A went further by creating four UI components (GhibliButton, WatercolorCard, TotoroAvatar, CloudBackground) and wiring time-of-day scene switching into HomeView — pulling work forward from Day 2. Build passes, 12/12 tests pass. The 5% gap: TotoroAvatar blink uses `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` instead of spec-recommended `Timer.publish`, and HomeView has two raw font literals that bypass the `GhibliFonts` tokens A created. Neither is blocking.\n18\t\n19\t### Alignment with spec\n20\t- ✅ Milestone Day 1 (skeleton + models + theme): All three delivered. Models match §5 field definitions. Colors match §3.1 hex values with two tasteful additions (noonSky, nightDeep) for scene switching.\n21\t- ✅ Aesthetic / UX: Theme tokens used consistently in new components. Font sizes match spec (title 32, body 22, button 24, clock 76). ButtonPressStyle