{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KY5ha2iYUk1eRL1ppARonx","type":"tool_result","content":"460\t| 外部連結 | App 內**不可有**任何連到網站、Email、社群的按鈕（除非在 parental gate 後面） |\n461\t| 行銷 / 升級提示 | 不可有 IAP 或「升級高級版」提示 |\n462\t| 第三方角色 | 不可使用龍貓、千尋等角色形象（會被告或被退）→ 自己畫「致敬風格」 |\n463\t| 角色名稱 | App 名 SunnyWake OK，但宣傳文案別寫「宮崎駿風」「Ghibli style」→ 寫「水彩手繪風」 |\n464\t\n465\t---\n466\t\n467\t## 7. 開發里程碑（建議 3 週 MVP）\n468\t\n469\t### Week 1：學習 + 骨架\n470\t- Day 1–2：跑 Apple 官方 SwiftUI Tutorial（Landmarks）\n471\t- Day 3：建專案、設定 Info.plist、跑 ContentView\n472\t- Day 4–5：寫 `Alarm` model + `AlarmListView`（純 UI，無功能）\n473\t- Day 6–7：寫 `AlarmScheduler`，能成功收到一個 local notification\n474\t\n475\t### Week 2：核心功能\n476\t- Day 8–9：`AudioRecorder` + `AudioPlayer`，能錄能播\n477\t- Day 10–11：`SpeechRecognizer`，console 印出辨識文字\n478\t- Day 12：串起 `AlarmRingView` 流程（聽到關鍵字→停止）\n479\t- Day 13–14：`ParentalGateView` + Settings flow\n480\t\n481\t### Week 3：美化 + 上架\n482\t- Day 15–16：套 Ghibli 視覺（背景、字型、按鈕、龍貓 avatar）\n483\t- Day 17：加 `ConfettiSwiftUI` + 樹葉飄落動畫\n484\t- Day 18：iPad layout 適配（用 `@Environment(\\.horizontalSizeClass)`）\n485\t- Day 19：實機測試（早上真的 set 7 點看會不會響）\n486\t- Day 20：上架素材（icon、screenshot、preview video）\n487\t- Day 21：送審（審查通常 24–48 小時，被退件就改）\n488\t\n489\t---\n490\t\n491\t## 8. 風險與備案\n492\t\n493\t| 風險 | 機率 | 備案 |\n494\t|---|---|---|\n495\t| 自訂音檔超過 30s 通知截斷 | 高 | 進前景後改用 AVAudioPlayer 長播 |\n496\t| 孩子根本不會講「我起床了」 | 中 | 提供「按大按鈕」備案，3 次語音失敗自動切按鈕模式 |\n497\t| 兒童類審查被退 | 中 | 不掛兒童類，改一般 Lifestyle，但年齡分級照標 |\n498\t| 繁中 on-device 辨識準確度低 | 低 | iOS 16+ 已支援，實測台灣腔 OK；備用簡中模型 |\n499\t| 龍貓造型被質疑抄襲 | 低–中 | 找插畫師原創「圓肚森林精靈」，避開耳朵與肚紋特徵 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"162e4724-11c2-4fa8-9f0d-e11f72ce045c","uuid":"5c83cc38-9c16-4eab-af8f-cac9e613bf57","timestamp":"2026-05-31T17:52:00.252Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lion/Documents/SunnyWalker/docs/swift_native_spec.md","content":"| 外部連結 | App 內**不可有**任何連到網站、Email、社群的按鈕（除非在 parental gate 後面） |\n| 行銷 / 升級提示 | 不可有 IAP 或「升級高級版」提示 |\n| 第三方角色 | 不可使用龍貓、千尋等角色形象（會被告或被退）→ 自己畫「致敬風格」 |\n| 角色名稱 | App 名 SunnyWake OK，但宣傳文案別寫「宮崎駿風」「Ghibli style」→ 寫「水彩手繪風」 |\n\n---\n\n## 7. 開發里程碑（建議 3 週 MVP）\n\n### Week 1：學習 + 骨架\n- Day 1–2：跑 Apple 官方 SwiftUI Tutorial（Landmarks）\n- Day 3：建專案、設定 Info.plist、跑 ContentView\n- Day 4–5：寫 `Alarm` model + `AlarmListView`（純 UI，無功能）\n- Day 6–7：寫 `AlarmScheduler`，能成功收到一個 local notification\n\n### Week 2：核心功能\n- Day 8–9：`AudioRecorder` + `AudioPlayer`，能錄能播\n- Day 10–11：`SpeechRecognizer`，console 印出辨識文字\n- Day 12：串起 `AlarmRingView` 流程（聽到關鍵字→停止）\n- Day 13–14：`ParentalGateView` + Settings flow\n\n### Week 3：美化 + 上架\n- Day 15–16：套 Ghibli 視覺（背景、字型、按鈕、龍貓 avatar）\n- Day 17：加 `ConfettiSwiftUI` + 樹葉飄落動畫\n- Day 18：iPad layout 適配（用 `@Environment(\\.horizontalSizeClass)`）\n- Day 19：實機測試（早上真的 set 7 點看會不會響）\n- Day 20：上架素材（icon、screenshot、preview video）\n- Day 21：送審（審查通常 24–48 小時，被退件就改）\n\n---\n\n## 8. 風險與備案\n\n| 風險 | 機率 | 備案 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 自訂音檔超過 30s 通知截斷 | 高 | 進前景後改用 AVAudioPlayer 長播 |\n| 孩子根本不會講「我起床了」 | 中 | 提供「按大按鈕」備案，3 次語音失敗自動切按鈕模式 |\n| 兒童類審查被退 | 中 | 不掛兒童類，改一般 Lifestyle，但年齡分級照標 |\n| 繁中 on-device 辨識準確度低 | 低 | iOS 16+ 已支援，實測台灣腔 OK；備用簡中模型 |\n| 龍貓造型被質疑抄襲 | 低–中 | 找插畫師原創「圓肚森林精靈」，避開耳朵與肚紋特徵 |","numLines":40,"startLine":460,"totalLines":514}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GaruuepvUXkpxCRdt61pit","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me write the Day 9 review entry.\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. **Spec alignment**: Day 9 milestone per spec is \"Day 8-9: AudioRecorder + AudioPlayer, able to record and play\" (Week 2 items). The project has already completed ALL of Week 2 items and most of Week 3 items. Day 9 addressed:\n   - Audio polish (harmonic arpeggios for `.caf` files) \n   - `AudioPlayer` delegate auto-reset\n   - App icon placeholder (spec Day 20 scope)\n   - iPad layout first-pass (spec Day 18 scope)\n   \n   This represents pulling forward approximately 10 days of spec work. The project is clearly ahead of schedule.\n\n2. **Code quality**: The audio player correctly implements the `nonisolated` pattern with `Task @MainActor` for delegate callbacks, and the delegate assignment happens at the right point after instantiation. The home view properly splits the layout for iPad using an `HStack` with clean dependency injection for the alarm check. Tests are in place and the long-press shortcut has been removed as expected.\n\n3. **Process**: All deliverables came through cleanly with an accurate prediction of validation results and no unexpected new files. The missing `AVFoundation` import was caught correctly, the fix was applied and validated, and the commit used the proper `[BROKEN-FIXED]` prefix.\n\n4. **For Day 10 brief**: With the project running 9-10 days ahead of schedule, the focus should shift toward visual enhancements—animating the CloudBackground, adding programmatic watercolor gradients to DaytimeScene, and making TotoroAvatar more expressive. ConfettiSwiftUI should be integrated into RewardView per the spec, the lingering `sampleAlarms` ModelContext issue needs resolution, and real-device testing prep should begin. The schedule buffer allows for this polish work before hitting the later milestones.\n\nGiven that true Ghibli-style artwork requires actual design work beyond what can be generated programmatically, the practical Day 10 priorities are ConfettiSwiftUI integration from the SPM package, smoothing out CloudBackground animations, fixing the `sampleAlarms` fragility, improving the time-based Totoro animations in AlarmRingView, and preparing a test checklist with proper Info.plist configuration for real-device testing.\n\nLet me check what the spec actually says about ConfettiSwiftUI in section 3.3 and where we stand with it currently.\n\nLooking back at the Day 4 and Day 5 reviews, I see that the team chose to implement pure SwiftUI confetti using deterministic star particles with staggered delays instead of pulling in the ConfettiSwiftUI package—and that was the right call since ConfettiSwiftUI is a third-party dependency that adds unnecessary complexity when a clean SwiftUI solution already works.\n\nFor the Day 10 brief, I'm thinking through several improvements: reconsidering ConfettiSwiftUI since the spec explicitly mentions it as acceptable and the current 20-star overlay, while functional, doesn't quite capture the dynamic confetti effect the spec envisions; adding smooth infinite-loop drift animations to the cloud background; replacing the fragile 7-day-old sample alarms model with a struct-based preview; implementing the voice fallback button logic from spec §8 that switches to button mode after three speech failures; and handling iPad landscape layouts properly instead of relying on a simple HStack.\n\nLooking at the risk register, the core issue is that children may struggle with the wake phrase, so the spec's mitigation is exactly what I need to build—after three failed recognition attempts, show a large tactile button that bypasses voice entirely. This fallback isn't implemented yet but it's critical for the app to actually work in real conditions.\n\nFor Day 10, I'm prioritizing: the voice fallback button in Alar